[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.42]
% tikz-3dplot hand-projected solid, not to scale
\draw (0.000,0.000)--(10.000,0.000)--(13.000,2.200);
\draw[dashed] (13.000,2.200)--(3.000,2.200)--(0.000,0.000);
\draw (6.500,13.100)--(0.000,0.000);
\draw (6.500,13.100)--(10.000,0.000);
\draw (6.500,13.100)--(13.000,2.200);
\draw[dashed] (6.500,13.100)--(3.000,2.200);
\draw[dashed] (6.500,13.100)--(6.500,1.100) node[midway,right] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\draw[dashed] (6.500,1.100)--(5.000,0.000);
\node[below] at (5.000,0.000) {$M$};
\draw (0.000,0.000)--(10.000,0.000) node[midway,below] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\node[below left] at (0.000,0.000) {$P$};
\node[below right] at (10.000,0.000) {$Q$};
\node[right] at (13.000,2.200) {$R$};
\node[left] at (3.000,2.200) {$S$};
\node[above] at (6.500,13.100) {$T$};
\node[below right] at (6.500,1.100) {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The square pyramid has base side $10$ cm and perpendicular height $12$ cm, with $M$ the midpoint of a base edge.
Find the angle that a side face makes with the base, correct to the nearest degree.

