Find the angle this plane makes with the base, correct to the nearest degree.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\coordinate (C) at (0,0);
\coordinate (T) at (0,2.3);
\coordinate (A) at (-0.8,-2.0);
\coordinate (B) at (2.35,-0.7);
\draw (C)--(A);
\draw (C)--(B);
\draw (A)--(T);
\draw (B)--(T);
\draw[red,thick] (T)--(C) node[midway,left] {$150\text{ m}$};
\coordinate (ra) at ($(C)!0.32cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (rb) at ($(C)!0.32cm!(B)$);
\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(C)$)--(rb);
\pic[draw,"$30^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.7cm,angle eccentricity=1.55] {angle=C--A--T};
\pic[draw,"$40^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.7cm,angle eccentricity=1.55] {angle=T--B--C};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,-0.1)--(0,1.05) node[above right] {N};
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above] at (T) {$T$};
\node[below right] at (C) {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A tower $TC$ is $150$ m tall.
From $A$, due south of the tower, the angle of elevation of the top is $30^{\circ}$; from $B$, due east, it is $40^{\circ}$.
Find the distance $AB$, to the nearest metre.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (-1.638,-1.147);
\coordinate (B) at (-1.491,2.130);
\draw (A)--(O);
\draw (B)--(O);
\coordinate (ra) at ($(O)!0.28cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (rb) at ($(O)!0.28cm!(B)$);
\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(O)$)--(rb);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (A)--($(A)+(0,1.1)$) node[above] {N};
\draw ($(A)+(90:0.75)$) arc (90:35:0.75);
\node at ($(A)+(62.5:1.05)$) {$055^{\circ}\text{T}$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (B)--($(B)+(0,1.1)$) node[above] {N};
\draw ($(B)+(90:0.75)$) arc (90:-55:0.75);
\node at ($(B)+(17.5:1.15)$) {$145^{\circ}\text{T}$};
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above left] at (B) {$B$};
\node[below right] at (O) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A $120$ m building stands at $O$.
From $A$ it is on a bearing of $055^{\circ}$T with the top at an angle of elevation of $38^{\circ}$; from $B$ it is on a bearing of $145^{\circ}$T with an angle of elevation of $30^{\circ}$.
Find the distance $AB$, to the nearest metre.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\coordinate (B) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (0,-2.2);
\coordinate (Q) at (2.2,0);
\draw[dashed] (P)--(B)--(Q);
\draw (P)--(Q) node[midway,above right] {$80\text{ m}$};
\coordinate (ra) at ($(B)!0.28cm!(P)$);
\coordinate (rb) at ($(B)!0.28cm!(Q)$);
\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(B)$)--(rb);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (P)--($(P)+(0,1.0)$) node[above left] {N};
\draw ($(P)+(0,0.8)$) arc (90:45:0.8);
\node at ($(P)+(0.21,0.51)$) {$35^{\circ}$};
\node[below] at (P) {$P$};
\node[right] at (Q) {$Q$};
\node[above left] at (B) {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A vertical pole stands at $B$.
Observer $P$ is due south and observer $Q$ due east of the pole.
$P$ and $Q$ are $80$ m apart, the bearing of $Q$ from $P$ is $035^{\circ}$, and the angle of elevation of the top of the pole from $Q$ is $32^{\circ}$.
Find the height of the pole, to the nearest metre.

